# rg.in — radius of gyration of the protein
#
# Rg measures how far the mass is spread around the centre of mass: lower means
# more compact. Unlike RMSD it needs no reference structure — it is a property
# of each frame on its own. Used here as a control: a stable Rg means the
# protein kept its fold, so any ligand behaviour is the ligand's, not the
# protein coming apart.
#
# Usage: cpptraj -i rg.in > rg.log 2>&1
# Replace SYSTEM, REP and NRES before running.

parm SYSTEM_dry.prmtop

# Full trajectory, no stride — radgyr is fast (seconds), unlike surf.
trajin SYSTEM_prod_REP_dry.nc

# Protein only; the ligand is the last residue and is left out so the value
# refers to the protein alone.
#   mass  = mass-weighted, the conventional definition
#   nomax = suppress the extra "max distance from centre" column, which would
#           otherwise make the output three columns instead of two
radgyr rg :1-NRES out rg_REP.dat mass nomax

go
